From 0b0c55f1647760eae8999f89ee19d500ed2975ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fi3 <you@example.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 14:18:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ADD backend command routing for selected-agent slash
 messages

Selected-agent slash chat is routed through a provider-native command hook instead of the normal model-send path. The default backend implementation reports unsupported commands without sending model input, while Codex maps supported slash commands to app-server command actions for the active thread.
---
 docs/architecture.md  |   6 ++
 src/agent_runtime.rs  |  17 ++++-
 src/cli.rs            |  31 +++++++++
 src/codex.rs          | 102 +++++++++++++++++------------
 src/workspace.rs      | 145 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/agent_core.rs   |   4 +-
 tests/terminal_app.rs |  37 +++++++++--
 tests/workspace.rs    |  61 ++++++++++++++----
 8 files changed, 340 insertions(+), 63 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index e319204..5ed506a 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -170,6 +170,10 @@ rather than using `@work-leaf` read, patch, or lock directives.
 
 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::execute_command` executes a provider-native command for an existing session
+  without routing the command text through the normal model-send path. Providers that do not expose
+  native commands use the default unsupported-command reply, so external providers can keep existing
+  implementations while adding command support only when they have a provider-specific command API.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
@@ -304,6 +308,8 @@ The primary public methods are:
   `launch_prepared_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven launch flows.
 - `CommandChat::send_to_agent`, `send_to_agent_streaming`, and
   `send_to_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven message flows.
+- `CommandChat::execute_agent_command` for provider-native commands routed from selected-agent
+  slash messages.
 - `CommandChat::shutdown_agents` and `shutdown_handle` for lifecycle cleanup.
 
 `CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.
